That's the classic symptom of an interval that is never cleared: every mount starts a new `setInterval` while the old ones keep running. Return a cleanup function from the effect:

```jsx
function Timer() {
  const [seconds, setSeconds] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    const id = setInterval(() => {
      setSeconds((s) => s + 1);
    }, 1000);
    return () => clearInterval(id);
  }, []);

  return <p>{seconds}s</p>;
}
```

React runs the cleanup when the component unmounts and before re-running the effect, so only one interval is ever alive. Also note `setSeconds((s) => s + 1)`: with `[]` as dependencies, `setSeconds(seconds + 1)` would keep reading `seconds` from the first render and get stuck at 1.

